<title>USA: Sparks - Larger US corn and soy crops, wheat down.</title>
<headline>Sparks - Larger US corn and soy crops, wheat down.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. corn and soybean output will climb from last year's levels but wheat will dip, according to Sparks Companies Inc projections Tuesday.</p>
<p>In remarks prepared for Agriculture Department's annual Outlook Forum, Sparks analyst Brad Anderson put 1997 U.S. corn plantings at 81.5 million acres and the crop at 9.6 billion bushels.</p>
<p>Wheat sowings were set at 70 million acres and output at 2.442 billion bushels.</p>
<p>Soybean acreage would be 64.5 million and output 2.45 billion bushels, according to the Sparks projections.</p>
</text>
